.TH CLONER 1 "October 2026" "cloner" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cloner \- clone git repositories structured for git worktree workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cloner
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIREPOSITORY\fR [\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cloner
is a wrapper around \fBgit clone\fR and \fBgit worktree\fR designed to facilitate
clean worktree workflows.
.PP
Instead of cloning directly into a working directory, \fBcloner\fR creates a parent
directory containing a bare repository in \fB.git\fR, configures remote tracking
branches for subsequent worktrees, and adds an initial worktree corresponding
to the remote default branch (or a branch explicitly specified).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-branch " \fINAME\fR"
Specify the branch to check out in the initial worktree. If omitted, \fBcloner\fR
automatically detects the remote default branch.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-error progress messages.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VERBOSITY
Integer controlling verbosity (default: 10). Set to 0 for quiet operation.
.SH EXAMPLES
Clone a repository into a directory named after the repo and check out its default branch:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cloner git@github.com:joshuacox/cloner.git
.fi
.RE
.PP
Clone into a custom directory name:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cloner git@github.com:joshuacox/cloner.git my_cloner
.fi
.RE
.PP
Clone and check out a specific branch:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cloner --branch develop git@github.com:joshuacox/cloner.git
.fi
.RE
